**EXCERPT FROM THE MERCHANDISING AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT AGREEMENT**

**THIS AGREEMENT** is made as of the 1st day of November, 2023, by and between **Retail Innovations Inc.**, located at 450 Commerce Way, Suite 300, Atlanta, GA 30339 (hereinafter referred to as "Retail Innovations"), and **E-Comm Solutions LLC**, located at 123 Digital Drive, San Francisco, CA 94105 (hereinafter referred to as "E-Comm Solutions").

**1. INVENTORY MANAGEMENT AND E-COMMERCE INTEGRATION**  
1.1 Retail Innovations shall utilize the **SmartStock Inventory Management System** (hereinafter referred to as "SmartStock") to oversee the inventory of all merchandise sold through its brick-and-mortar locations and its e-commerce platform, www.retailinnovations.com.  
1.2 E-Comm Solutions shall integrate its proprietary **E-Comm Connect API** into SmartStock to ensure real-time synchronization of inventory levels between Retail Innovations’ physical stores and online sales, with a target latency of no more than 2 seconds.

**2. CUSTOMER SERVICE COLLABORATION**  
2.1 Retail Innovations agrees to employ a dedicated customer service team, led by **Jane Doe**, Customer Service Manager, to handle all inquiries arising from e-commerce transactions.  
2.2 E-Comm Solutions will provide training resources and ongoing support to Retail Innovations' customer service team, ensuring that representatives can effectively manage an estimated 500 customer interactions per day, which include product inquiries, order status updates, and return processing.

**3. MERCHANDISING STRATEGY**  
3.1 Both parties shall collaborate on a quarterly basis, with the next meeting scheduled for the 15th of January, 2024, to assess sales performance metrics derived from SmartStock and E-Comm Connect.  
3.2 Retail Innovations shall provide E-Comm Solutions with access to sales data indicating trends in merchandise movement, which will inform strategic decisions related to stock reordering and promotional activities.

**4. TERM AND TERMINATION**  
4.1 This Agreement shall commence on the date first written above and shall remain in effect for one year, unless terminated earlier by either party with a written notice of 30 days.  
4.2 In the event of a material breach of this Agreement, either party may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect if such breach remains uncured for a period of 15 days following written notice.

